{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a metal-free, organophotocatalyzed Csp3-Csp2 cross-coupling reaction between alkyl carboxylic acids and beta-aryl-vinyl halides using the organic dye 4CzIPN. The reaction is highly stereoselective, initially yielding E-alkenes through a decarboxylative radical addition-elimination mechanism. Prolonged irradiation allows for in situ E-to-Z isomerization via energy transfer, providing divergent access to both stereoisomers.",
